EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
       DDEEBB__BBUUIILLDD__OOPPTTIIOONNSS
           This variable can be used to enable or disable various features
           that affect the information included in the .buildinfo file, via
           the bbuuiillddiinnffoo option (since dpkg 1.18.19).  This option contains a
           comma-separated list of features, prefixed with the '++' or '--'
           modifiers, to denote whether to enable or disable them.  The
           special feature "aallll" can be used to enable or disable all other
           features.  The feature "ppaatthh" controls whether to unconditionally
           include the BBuuiilldd--PPaatthh field.

       DDPPKKGG__CCOOLLOORRSS
           Sets the color mode (since dpkg 1.18.5).  The currently accepted
           values are: aauuttoo (default), aallwwaayyss and nneevveerr.

       DDPPKKGG__NNLLSS
           If set, it will be used to decide whether to activate Native
           Language Support, also known as internationalization (or i18n)
           support (since dpkg 1.19.0).  The accepted values are: 00 and 11
           (default).

FFIILLEESS
       ddeebbiiaann//ffiilleess
           The list of generated files.  ddppkkgg--ggeennbbuuiillddiinnffoo reads the data here
           when producing a ..bbuuiillddiinnffoo file.

